{
 "name": "wedge_nose",
 "description": "Generator v2: 'wedge-nose' seesaw car (passive plank presser).\n\nA compact rear-drive car whose nose is a pair of 36.9 deg liftarm wedges\n(3-4-5 triangle: 10 holes = 64 mm along, 48 mm up). Driving forward, the raised\nnear end of the plank meets the underside of the wedges and slides down them,\nso the drive itself tips the plank near-end-down onto its ledge; the wedges'\nlow ends (6.8 mm up, just ahead of the front wheels) keep it down until the\nfront wheels roll onto it and the car's weight holds it. The car climbs, the\nplank tips under it at the axle, and it drives down onto the goal platform.\n\nDrive: M motor across the chassis between the rails, outboard 1:5 train\n(24T->40T, 8T->24T) to the rear axle. AAA battery sits over the rear axle on\ntwo upper rails; IR receiver on the battery.",
 "chassis": "rail_l",
 "motor": "motor",
 "battery": "battery",
